            <h2 id="rolling-cart-title">15 Drawers Rolling Cart, Classroom Organizers</h2>
            <p class="product-subtitle">A mobile home for materials, stations, and student work</p>
            <p>This style of rolling cart is useful when a classroom has plenty of materials but they are hard to find at the moment of instruction. Different drawer sizes and colors make it easy to organize by class, unit, project, or activity type, while the wheels let the cart move between a planning area, teaching space, and student station.</p>

            <h3>Why I recommend it</h3>
            <div class="product-reasons">
              <section><strong>Large drawers hold complete sets</strong><p>Store worksheets, student projects, printable games, lab sheets, art materials, or work waiting to be reviewed. A different color for each class makes retrieval faster.</p></section>
              <section><strong>Small drawers sort loose supplies</strong><p>Keep cards, dice, magnets, markers, sticky notes, manipulatives, and exit tickets in a consistent place that students can help maintain.</p></section>
              <section><strong>It can become a learning station</strong><p>Use the top for a task basket or demonstration materials, then roll the cart to a small group to reduce time spent passing out supplies.</p></section>
            </div>

            <div class="product-teacher-tip"><strong>Classroom use tip:</strong><span> Place heavier paper and supplies in the lower drawers and lighter items near the top. Add word-and-picture labels so students can return materials independently. Lock the wheels before use, and remind students not to climb on the cart or pull out several full drawers at once.</span></div>

